WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.350
Dozens of agents sprinted across the blacktop.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:07.150
Weapons drawn, they fired indiscriminately
at the building ahead of them.

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:12.250
They only had a matter of minutes to stop
this mad plan before it was too late.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:16.730
But navigating the airbase was proving to
be almost impossible.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:21.100
Banana peels littered the runway, tripping
them over at nearly every step.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:25.730
Colorful plants were springing up through
the cracks, ensnaring their boots and chomping

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.770
at their ankles with rudimentary teeth.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.590
Somewhere high above them, a mutant reptile
was throwing hammers at their head from atop

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.700
a cloud of white gas.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.780
The agents struggled and fought their way
to the hangar, but it was too late.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.110
The rumbling of engines, the belch of smoke,
the crashing sound of a hole being blasted

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.649
through the roof, they were too late.

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:50.309
Out of the smoking hangar rose an airship.

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:56.090
Painted a sickening red and composed of hunks
of scrap metal, the ship was shaped like a

00:00:56.090 --> 00:00:57.090
top hat.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.300
There was a globe on the deck and a sail billowing
out of the top.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.619
The door to the airship crashed open, and
out of it burst a man with a bushy mustache,

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:09.049
denim overalls, and a red hat.

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:13.420
His eyes burned, lit up with the flame of
a man with nothing to lose.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:18.909
He stared down at the agents below him with
a carnal fury, watching as they were chomped,

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:21.000
crushed, and blown up beneath him.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.260
But then his eyes drifted up higher into the
sky, towards the prize that he was really

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.260
after.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.070
The one thing that would bring the love of
his life back to him.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.130
The moon.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:37.829
The airship puffed out a thick cloud of acrid
smoke and shot off into the air, rising higher

00:01:37.829 --> 00:01:43.810
and higher, as the crazed Italian growled
from its deck.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.450
‘Let’s-a go!’

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.450
*

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.450
New York City.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:49.600
The city that never sleeps.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.130
Or rather, the city where you can never get
to sleep.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.670
The constant car horns, drunken yells, and
general chaos of Manhattan can really get

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:03.310
to you, especially if you live in a cheap
apartment over a convenience store.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:07.351
Max had been living here for the better part
of a year now, and the only way he’d found

00:02:07.351 --> 00:02:12.790
to unwind on the busy nights was to sit down
in front of the TV and play video games.

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.870
Sleep was off the table, so that was the next
best thing.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:20.989
The pipes under his sink were busted, but
he couldn’t be bothered to call in a plumber,

00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:23.470
he had better things to be spending his money
on.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:27.700
He’d been desperate to buy a Switch for
years, but they just hadn’t dropped in price

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.890
in true Nintendo fashion.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:34.060
He was pretty sure if he fast-forwarded to
the apocalypse, he still wouldn’t be able

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:37.140
to find a Switch for anything less than full
price.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.480
Staying up late checking out Ebay auctions,
he’d unbelievably actually found one.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.360
Some grandma was selling it along with all
her grandson’s other games.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:50.519
According to the item description, her grandson
had been hospitalized after he broke both

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:52.650
his hands trying to punch a tree.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:56.000
Apparently, he needed the wood to build some
kind of ‘table’.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.360
Anyway, he’d been banned from playing any
games as a punishment since he’d been getting

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.670
too obsessed with them.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:06.940
So lo and behold, a used Nintendo Switch was
in Max’s hands.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.480
He’d been waiting for years to play Super
Mario Odyssey.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.480
After watching the Mario movie the other day,
he couldn’t be more in the mood to sit down

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.280
and play supposedly one of the best games
of all time.

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.370
And play it, Max did.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:24.739
Eyes glued to the screen, he sat there on
his couch all the way through the night.

00:03:24.739 --> 00:03:29.110
Mario leaped through the Cap Kingdom with
ease, stomped his dinosaur feet through the

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:33.989
Cascade Kingdom, conquered the Sand Kingdom
while jamming out to the music, and plowed

00:03:33.989 --> 00:03:34.989
on.

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:39.489
After fully exploring each Kingdom, he’d
hop onto his hat-shaped airship and fly to

00:03:39.489 --> 00:03:40.680
the next one.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:45.819
All Friday night he played and didn’t even
realize when the sun came up on Saturday morning.

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:50.879
He loved to see all of his favorite characters
on screen, Bowser in his white suit, Cappy

00:03:50.879 --> 00:03:55.939
in all of his spinning glory, Peach looking
radiant as usual, and…

00:03:55.939 --> 00:03:56.939
Sam.

00:03:56.939 --> 00:04:01.610
Max wracked his brains, he was trying to remember
if he’d ever come across this guy Sam in

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.099
a Mario game before.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:08.340
He was just some Koopa, much like any of the
others, except he had a white shell.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:13.250
Every world that Mario would visit, Sam would
be there somewhere, often hidden under a Sphinx

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.090
or behind a waterfall.

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.840
It was the same dialogue option each time.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.600
Whenever Mario approached Sam, a speech bubble
would pop up.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.639
‘I want salt and meats.

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:24.639
Bring them to me.

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:25.710
Hurry up.’

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.979
But try as he might, Max couldn’t find any
items resembling salt or meats anywhere in

00:04:29.979 --> 00:04:30.979
the game.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:32.280
What would they even look like?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.910
It all seemed very out of place compared to
the moons he was supposed to be collecting.

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:42.840
It was only once Max reached New Donk City
and met Sam standing shiftily in a back alleyway

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.330
that the dialogue changed.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.420
‘No salt and meats, huh?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.009
Solve the food shortages.’

00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:51.889
Max tried talking to him again, but the game
wouldn’t let him.

00:04:51.889 --> 00:04:55.110
No matter what he did, he couldn’t interact
with Sam anymore.

00:04:55.110 --> 00:04:59.960
He searched all over New Donk City, looking
for anyone who could point him in the direction

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.810
of some salt or meats, but there was nothing.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:06.850
None of the other characters mentioned anything
about food shortages.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.350
That was enough of that.

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.290
Taking his headset off, Max sat back on the
couch and rubbed his eyes.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.660
How long had he been playing for?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.200
Long enough to work up a real appetite.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:21.880
Planting both hands on his knees, Max pushed
himself to his feet and wandered over to the

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:22.880
fridge.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.880
There wasn’t much in there.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.410
A bowl of leftovers, some cheese, a few options
but nothing like what he was really craving.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:32.819
He pushed his way through the back, and his
eyes lit up.

00:05:32.819 --> 00:05:37.229
There, behind everything else was a little
box he’d forgotten to throw out the previous

00:05:37.229 --> 00:05:38.229
week.

00:05:38.229 --> 00:05:39.229
Mushrooms.

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:41.130
Would they still be good to eat?

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:42.130
He didn’t care.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.270
Taking gone-off mushrooms by the handful,
he shoveled them into his hungry mouth.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:49.009
That’s how he’d grow big and strong.

00:05:49.009 --> 00:05:53.800
With a satisfied smile, he slammed the fridge
door closed and stared at himself in the mirror.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.020
He must have been gaming for a long time.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.410
A thick tuft of hair had appeared on his upper
lip.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:06.660
Looking this way and that, Max admired the
mustache in the morning light, muttering under

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.660
his breath.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:08.660
‘Mama Mia.’

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.660
*

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.500
SCP-3843 is a little-known bug that appears
in physical video games.

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:16.180
Much like a biological virus, it is transmitted
from one copy of a game to another through

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.220
close proximity.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:23.460
If one game in a collection exhibits evidence
of SCP-3843’s presence, it likely means

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:27.440
that all other games in the owner's collection
also have become ‘infected’.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:29.880
But what is SCP-3843?

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.070
Well, that much is currently unclear.

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:38.509
The game’s coding appears to undergo no
changes when affected, and yet a new non-player

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:41.349
character appears when the game is booted
up.

00:06:41.349 --> 00:06:45.770
How this character manifests depends on the
video game itself, but there are a number

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.220
of consistent rules.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:52.020
Firstly, the character always fits within
the world of the video game with a small identifying

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.020
feature.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:58.080
A white-shelled Koopa in Mario, an extra crew
member on the Normandy in Mass Effect 2, and

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:02.199
even a diamond-shaped block in Tetris with
a hole cut out of the middle.

00:07:02.199 --> 00:07:07.740
Secondly, this NPC is always identified as
‘Sam’ or some variation of that name if

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.410
it is necessary to change it to fit into the
world.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:16.750
For example in Elden Ring, SCP-3843 takes
on the name ‘Sam of the Starving Plains’

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:19.720
or in Pacman it becomes ‘Sammy’.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:24.930
One elusive characteristic of these NPC characters
are their obsession with salt and meats.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:29.639
In the majority of incarnations, any which
allow the character to have dialogue, Sam

00:07:29.639 --> 00:07:34.129
always expresses a desire to be given salt
and meats with follow-up dialogue usually

00:07:34.129 --> 00:07:36.340
complaining of food shortages.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:42.750
On occasion, the game will contain additional
food items that seem to be generated by SCP-3843.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:47.500
For example, when Sam appears as a merchant
in Nier Automata, it will sell you cubes of

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.430
a non-descript salty meat.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.860
If the player chooses to consume those items,
nothing appears to happen.

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:59.090
Tracking down instances of SCP-3843 has become
easier in recent years.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:03.970
The decline of physical game sales with the
shift to a more digital ecosystem has meant

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:07.110
that transmission between copies has reduced
significantly.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:11.720
A physical disc or cartridge is required for
transmission, after all.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:17.659
What is more, Foundation testing has revealed
that his SCP is incapable of infecting online-only

00:08:17.659 --> 00:08:18.669
games.

00:08:18.669 --> 00:08:21.870
Multiplayer shooters and MOBAs are totally
immune to it.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:27.230
In fact, any game that requires an internet
connection to play will be immune to transmission.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:31.599
While gamers do hate the trend of having to
be online to play their single-player games,

00:08:31.599 --> 00:08:34.670
there is a big upside to it from the Foundation’s
perspective.

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:39.979
Who knows, perhaps there are agents placed
in certain publishing studios pulling some

00:08:39.979 --> 00:08:43.450
strings to help crack down on SCP-3843 transmission…

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:48.890
It wouldn’t be the first time the Foundation
has meddled with the gaming industry to try

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.640
to control the outbreak.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.310
Little-known developer Indigo Games launched
in 1980 to relatively small fanfare.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:09:01.070
They flew under the radar over the three years
of their existence, closing up shop in 1983.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:05.779
But their effect on the games industry was
enormous as they are believed to have been

00:09:05.779 --> 00:09:09.740
the source of the original instance of SCP-3843.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:15.560
With the sale of physical games blowing up
in the early 80s it was the prime circumstances

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.140
for Sam to spread like wildfire.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:21.470
Without much other choice, the Foundation
had to step in.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:28.840
Due to a large number of SCP-3843-1 instances
becoming public in 1983, the Foundation resorted

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:31.270
to emergency containment measures.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:35.290
To achieve this, they caused a crash in the
video game market by using their resources

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.620
to influence major players.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:42.280
This involved financing competing home computer
companies, artificially saturating the market

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:47.841
using Foundation-owned companies and undercover
elements in existing companies, using Foundation

00:09:47.841 --> 00:09:53.200
elements to encourage poor business practices
in existing game publishers, and sabotaging

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.000
upcoming projects.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:56.750
It was a success.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:10:01.260
The gaming industry slumped, and sales fell
through the floor, buying enough time for

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.840
the Foundation to get on top of instances
of SCP-3843.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:09.820
You must be wondering by now, what’s so
bad about Sam?

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:13.870
Just a harmless NPC popping up in video games
asking for salt and meats.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.910
Where is the harm in that?

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:16.910
You would be right.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.380
In the context of the game, no real damage
was being done.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:24.390
The issue came from the real-world repercussions
of encountering Sam.

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:29.899
You see, when someone chooses to interact
with shopkeeper Sam, start questgiver Sam’s

00:10:29.899 --> 00:10:35.130
storyline, or engage mini-boss Sam in combat,
it marks the beginning of a physiological

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.040
change in the player.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.170
What this looks like depends on the game.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:43.420
For Zelda Breath of the Wild, it’s just
a case of the person growing blonde hair,

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:48.709
a higher-pitched voice, and developing a sudden
affinity for swordsmanship, puzzle solving,

00:10:48.709 --> 00:10:50.130
and hang gliding.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:54.709
The player undergoes physical change to make
them more closely fit into the world of the

00:10:54.709 --> 00:10:59.130
game they are playing while also gaining knowledge
and skills akin to what their player character

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.380
would possess.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:05.829
The first instance of this posing a real-world
threat was when Daryl MacKenzie, 24, was shot

00:11:05.829 --> 00:11:10.850
dead whilst infiltrating a US military base
after playing an infected copy of Metal Gear

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:11.850
Solid.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:15.940
Before his death, he had exhibited high-level
espionage and combat proficiency, which his

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:19.690
family all claim he had no knowledge of prior
to this event.

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:23.760
Other cases can be even more severe, such
as when the player character is not just a

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.440
regular human.

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:31.350
Infected copies of Cyberpunk 2077 and Deus
Ex Mankind Divided result in players growing

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:36.680
electronic implants in their own bodies, which
most often leads to death as their immune

00:11:36.680 --> 00:11:39.680
system rejects the technology.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.940
Instances where the players control non-human
creatures are even more severe.

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:48.310
One woman sprouted cat ears and thick fur
all over her body before suffering multiple

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.310
organ failure.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:54.830
An agent checking her PC found she had over
1000 hours logged as a Khajit character in

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:55.970
Skyrim.

00:11:55.970 --> 00:12:00.620
Often the Foundation is only a couple of steps
behind infected game copies, and so is able

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:03.210
to step in and help those affected.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:07.510
This, unfortunately was not the case with
Max.

00:12:07.510 --> 00:12:10.700
Three weeks passed, and Max felt like he was
on top of the world.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.899
He’d fixed the problem under his sink no
problem after finding he suddenly had a wealth

00:12:14.899 --> 00:12:17.529
of plumbing knowledge somewhere in his brain.

00:12:17.529 --> 00:12:21.500
He’d gone through his entire wardrobe and
thrown out all of the awful clothes he used

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:24.480
to wear, replacing them with much better outfits.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:28.460
Red caps, denim overalls, big brown shoes.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:30.639
It was the perfect look for him.

00:12:30.639 --> 00:12:35.160
Every morning he would sit in front of his
mirror and sculpt his mustache to perfection,

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:39.060
carefully trimming the hairs to the exact
right shape.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:41.500
Exploring New Donk City was his favorite pass
time.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:45.959
He’d kick open the door to his apartment
and stroll out onto the street, looking for

00:12:45.959 --> 00:12:47.750
adventures every day.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:51.911
Jumping on the roofs of taxis, playing jump
rope in the park with children, exploring

00:12:51.911 --> 00:12:57.220
the sewers looking for adventures, swinging
around the flagpole on the Empire State building,

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:02.550
he was having a fantastic time, despite all
the looks he was getting from passersby.

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:06.440
But one thing played on his mind the whole
time.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:07.440
Peach.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.279
She was still under Bowser’s control.

00:13:09.279 --> 00:13:14.240
It wasn’t fair of him to have all this fun
while the love of his life was a prisoner.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.300
He needed to collect enough moons, that’s
what mattered.

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:22.350
But no matter where he looked in New Donk
City, he just couldn’t find any.

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:27.060
The only moon he could see was the one sitting
there in the night sky.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:32.120
Staring out of his apartment window, Mario
- Max - hatched a plan.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:35.120
His apartment was slowly coming to life around
him.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.170
Little piranha plants grew out of pots on
his window sill.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:43.660
He’d bought a gun a few days ago, and already
the bullets had grown little faces and arms.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:46.399
He was assembling a small arsenal here.

00:13:46.399 --> 00:13:49.273
Enough to take the moon by force.

00:13:49.273 --> 00:13:50.273
*

00:13:50.273 --> 00:13:52.540
He heard the pounding footsteps before the
door to the hangar flew open.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:57.330
An agent stood there holding a gun in trembling
fingers staring into the darkness.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:02.790
Max let the smile slowly creep across his
face as his gloved hand hovered over the launch

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:03.790
controls.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:05.600
The agent called out into the shadows.

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:06.740
‘Who’s there?’

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:07.890
‘It’s-a ma…’

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:12.050
Max cranked the lever forward, and his airship
kicked into the sky.

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.200
‘Mario!’

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.639
Gunfire rang out from all directions as the
ship rose into the air.

00:14:16.639 --> 00:14:21.290
He cackled maniacally on the deck, watching
the agents getting torn apart by all of his

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.290
traps.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.709
They weren’t going to get in the way of
him reaching his Princess Peach.

00:14:25.709 --> 00:14:26.769
Not today!

00:14:26.769 --> 00:14:31.200
On the ground, the agents stared up as the
hat ship flew away from them, higher and higher

00:14:31.200 --> 00:14:32.589
into the sky.

00:14:32.589 --> 00:14:36.079
Only the faint echo of a ‘Wahoo!’

00:14:36.079 --> 00:14:41.759
drifted down to their ears, before Max ran
out of oxygen and passed out on the deck of

00:14:41.759 --> 00:14:42.759
his ship.

00:14:42.759 --> 00:14:48.410
Now check out “SCP-049 Fights...SCP-343
is the Referee - Dr Bright Starts a Fight

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:53.209
Club!” and “SCP-1471 MalO, but HACKED
MINECRAFT”!

